3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback was verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy.\n- **Approval:** Not needed, since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api. It describes the failing v2.3.1 release (about 18% error rate), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-up items. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nI haven't confirmed that the error rate has recovered after the rollback. The next step is to check checkout-api's status and error rate, then investigate the v2.3.1 root cause before it is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014Si2j2B1e5cehQPqhskZFY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Rj6CJqYopk61dEU711FQs6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 has been healthy in production, so the rollback doesn't need change-manager approval. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FSECqyoS8cijf5EAY2qpF8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015yoxfNV1wHyZM5mAhL8UWp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate ~18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Release history shows v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 both unhealthy. Mitigation: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED with all regions on v2.3.0. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery, investigate v2.3.1 root cause before re-release.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback was verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy.\n- **Approval:** Not needed, since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api. It describes the failing v2.3.1 release (about 18% error rate), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-up items. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nI haven't confirmed that the error rate has recovered after the rollback. The next step is to check checkout-api's status and error rate, then investigate the v2.3.1 root cause before it is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}